    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Maffucci syndrome</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p><strong>A</strong>&nbsp;Hand deformity due to multiple enchondromas; note the superficial haemangioma. <strong>B</strong>&nbsp;In another patient, multiple enchondromas with and without soft tissue extension in the second to fifth digits and the fifth metacarpal bone. In addition, phleboliths (arrows) can be seen in the soft tissue at the bases of the second and fourth fingers, indicating haemangiomas.</p>",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "<p>Reprinted with permission from:</p>\r\n<p>Fletcher CDM, Bridge JA, Hogendoorn PCW, Mertens F (Eds): WHO Classification of Tumours of Soft Tissue and Bone. IARC: Lyon 2013</p>\r\n<p>and</p>\r\n<p>Pansuriya TC, Kroon HM, Bov&eacute;e JV. Enchondromatosis: insights on the different subtypes. Int J Clin Exp Pathol. 2010 Jun 26;3(6):557-69. PMID: 20661403</p>",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/33/200/8594.jpg",
